    "Typed Common dispel slow uses existing closed Dispelling/InfluenceRef and ordinary live permission, key+primitive/schema, resources and ticket checks. Trusted binding supplies identity without cast authority.",
    "Each active Slow owns monotonic instance, target generation, original immutable plan, effect index, onset/expiry and exact spoken caster/action or item generation/touch-fact provenance. Two casts and separate recipients remain distinguishable.",
    "Selective removal/expiry changes exactly one contribution, retaining other Slow, completed damage/heal, wards, payments, pending work and history. Duplicate Slow writes within one activation still refuse Overlap.",
    "Independent casts/items now combine by minimum active permille; aggregate until_tick is the earliest active expiry. statuses caps contributions at the existing default16. This explicitly supersedes blanket ActiveSlow refusal.",
    "Checkpoint owns active/pending/item plans, provenance and counter, validates coherent aggregates and historical/live generations before adoption, and renews incarnation-bound refs/tickets. Reused slots cannot retarget stale capabilities.",
    "Real ordinary caller proves hp46, remaining Slow500 until300, ward8 until400 and mana A60/B90 across original owner destruction and restore, then normal speed at300. Existing servant/pending/item contracts pass focused regressions."
  ],
